From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:28:04 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 227/230] Match detail: league title with round subtitle, named
 scoreboard, center-spine timeline
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TopBar title is now the competition name (subtitle = ESPN's cup round,
localized; league matches send no round/gameweek, so no placeholder
subtitle) and the round back-chevron next to it is gone. The scoreboard
puts the team name under each crest, the big score reads home-first
(first digit = the home side's goals, verified against Liverpool 2-0
Brighton whose timeline credits both goals to the home team id), the
live pill carries the minute, and the date/time sits below with the
clock isolated dir=ltr so bidi never scrambles. Tabs are underline style
with the same tab/panel aria wiring. Timeline is a center spine: minutes
centered, a goal's produced score under its own minute, home events on
the home column, away on the other, names wrap instead of truncating,
scorer bold with an assist ("پاس: …"), swap line for subs, yellow/red/
own-goal kinds localized. Stats tab localizes club names and Persian
digits. FA strings added for yellow/red/own goal/assist/XI; kickoff
renamed "شروع نیمه اول".

